  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 305 AM MST SUN NOV 8 2026\nAn upper level ridge centered to our east will amplify through \nlate week. The building ridge and increased southerly flow will \nincrease temperatures a few more degrees. This will place max \ntemperatures near daily record highs, and lower valleys are \nforecast to reach the mid to upper 60s and may approach 70F. A \ndeep upper level trough approaching the coast will split mid \nweek, with the southern portion closing off and diving south to \nsouthern California. The northern portion is favored to remain \noff the coast initially, continuing mild and dry conditions. \nHowever, some global ensemble members bring it inland enough \nfor a 10-30% chance of showers, with the highest chance across \nthe north and the mountains. Confidence is higher that the \ntrough will progress inland by Sunday or early next week, \nbringing the potential for widespread precipitation and cooler \ntemperatures. The amplified pattern will bring breezy south to \nsoutheasterly winds mid week, increasing late week into the \nweekend as the trough approaches.",
